    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This charming and character-filled home offers a wonderful blend of comfort, style, and potential, making it an ideal holiday retreat or the perfect property for those looking to downsize while remaining close to local amenities."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "The accommodation begins with a well-appointed galley kitchen featuring attractive fitted wooden units, which opens seamlessly into a spacious open-plan kitchen and sitting room. The cosy sitting area is centred around a wood-burning stove, creating a warm and welcoming atmosphere throughout the year.\r\n\r\nJust off the sitting room is a delightful lounge with extensive glazing, allowing natural light to flood the space and creating a bright, airy room that is perfect for relaxing or entertaining.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the first floor comprises three well-proportioned bedrooms and two bathrooms. The generous master bedroom is particularly bright and benefits from its own en-suite bathroom. Additional storage is available in a loft space accessed from one of the bedrooms.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property enjoys a lovely enclosed garden arranged over different levels, offering a private and attractive outdoor space with plenty of potential for gardening, relaxing, or alfresco dining.\r\n\r\nFull of charm and quirky character, this unique home is just a three-minute stroll from the town centre, where a wide range of shops, cafés, and amenities can be enjoyed. There is also convenient access to a public car park directly across the road, adding further practicality to this centrally located property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: F"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Location",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "This area of South West Ireland is of outstanding beauty with its dramatic coastline, unspoilt locations and safe beaches. The property is within easy walking distance of the dock beach, making it ideal for those who enjoy sea swimming.The Leisure activities are well catered for, Kinsale provides excellent sailing, yachting and fishing facilities from its two marinas. There are two world class golf courses including the renowned Old Head of Kinsale. Other recreational pursuits include walking, bathing, surfing, and horse riding.\r\n\r\nThere are numerous cultural events held throughout the year, such as the world famous Kinsale Arts Festival, the Cork Jazz Festival, Cork Film Festival, Kinsale Gourmet Festival along with a thriving music and opera programme. Cork has several fine theatres, and Cork Opera House hosts many exceptional productions throughout the year.\r\n\r\nKinsale is also home to some of Ireland’s finest restaurants, contributing to its title as Gourmet Capital of Ireland; along with many top class hotels and welcoming pubs.\r\n\r\nCork International Airport is conveniently located 20 minutes drive from Kinsale with direct links within Ireland and to major European and UK cities"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Disclaimer/Privacy Policy:",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Finest International Real Estate Ireland Ltd. t/a Engel & Voelkers act as agents for the vendors or lessors of this property whose agents they are, give notice that: \r\n1. By sending an enquiry through the property portal in relation to any of our property listings you are consenting to the storage, use and processing of your personal data by the provider according to Engel & Voelkers’ privacy policy in order for us to reply to your contact request or request for information. A copy of our privacy policy can be viewed at www.engelvoelkers.com/southkerry/privacypolicy. You can revoke your consent at any time in the future in line with the privacy policy.\r\n2. The particulars are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees, and do not institute, nor constitute part of, an offer or contract. \r\n3. All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for use and occupation, and any other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers or tenants should not rely on them as statements or representatives of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. \r\n4. Any loose furniture, non-integrated appliances, white goods and curtains are deemed not to be included in the sale of the property unless specifically agreed between the parties and outlined in an inventory. Any reference to appliances refers to integrated appliances only.\r\n5. No person in the employment of Finest International Real Estate Ireland Ltd. t/a Engel & Voelkers has any authority to make or give representation or warranty in relation to this property. \r\n6. Availability upon agreement - subject to contract. This offer is subject to change of price, withdrawal or prior sale without notice. \r\n7. Transfer fees, i.e. stamp duty, solicitor fees etc, are not included in the sales price and have to be paid by the buyer. The commission will be paid by the seller."
      }
